Focused Ion Beam systems use a concentrated ion beam to image, mill, etch, or deposit material with high precision. These capabilities make them important tools for semiconductor circuit editing, defect investigation, sample preparation, and advanced materials characterization. Combining focused ion beam technology with scanning electron microscopy enables detailed imaging alongside precise material removal.

The market benefits from increasing semiconductor complexity and the need to investigate defects at increasingly smaller dimensions. Research institutions and laboratories also use these systems for nanotechnology, materials science, and biological sample preparation.

