Market Challenges
High Equipment and Operating Costs
Focused ion beam systems require specialized components, precision engineering, and technical support. High acquisition and maintenance costs can limit adoption by smaller laboratories and research organizations.

Specialized Skills and Sample Preparation
Operating the equipment effectively requires trained personnel and carefully controlled workflows. Sample preparation can also be time-consuming, depending on the material and analysis requirements.

Market Restraints
Budget Constraints in Research and Manufacturing
Capital expenditure cycles and laboratory budgets can influence purchasing decisions. Some organizations may delay equipment replacement or rely on external analytical service providers instead of purchasing new systems.

